  "plan": {
    "goal": "Characterize the flow metrics (wall shear stress, residence time, channel volume, mean velocity) of a 650 µm × 54 µm × 9.1 mm microfluidic channel perfused at 4.59 µL/min with medium of viscosity 0.0035 Pa·s and density 1060 kg/m³.",
    "rationale": "Pure flow-characterization calculation for a rectangular microchannel. The wall shear stress, residence time, channel volume and mean velocity are all derived from the channel geometry (650 µm wide, 54 µm high, 9.1 mm long) and the perfusion flow rate (4.59 µL/min) with the stated medium properties (μ = 0.0035 Pa·s, ρ = 1060 kg/m³). The resulting wall shear stress (~0.85 Pa) sits at the upper end of the microvascular endothelial range (0.1–1 Pa) but well above hepatic sinusoidal shear (0.05–0.15 Pa); the flow is laminar (Re << 2300).",
